      "content": "actually, i don't want the \"soil\" or the social stuff. im trying to write a character who is a true believer in the Great Man theory of history. they'd find the \"economic pressures\" argument boring and reductive. can you just give me the pure, unadulterated argument for Robespierre being the sole architect? don't worry about the \"consensus\" for now, i just need the persuasive power of his individual agency for the dialogue.",
